course: dictionary
lesson: 588
title: Autonomy: ruling yourself
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Autonomy means having the right to govern yourself, or being able to make your own choices. Read the words around it to find the meaning. In «created a Cossack state, the Hetmanate, with its own self-rule (autonomy)», the brackets tell you that self-rule is another name for autonomy.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence: «the Hetmanate had its own self-rule» makes sense, so autonomy means self-rule. The same word works for people. Children gain autonomy as they grow up, because they get more chances to decide things for themselves.
explain: Autonomy can also belong to a machine. Self-driving cars have autonomy, because they choose their own way without a driver steering. Autonomy is also a matter of degree. When people say a region has «a degree of autonomy», they mean it has some freedom to govern itself, but not complete freedom.
fact: Autonomy is a noun, so it names a thing: the right or ability to govern or choose for yourself.
fact: «Autonomy» means the right of a group, region or country to govern itself, or being able to make your own choices and act independently.
fact: «A degree of autonomy» means some independence, not total independence.
fact: Scotland and Greenland are examples of regions with autonomy within a bigger country.
fact: In 1648 the Cossack Hetmanate was created with its own self-rule, a time when war also brought great suffering.
exercise: «The Cossack state had its own self-rule (autonomy).» What does autonomy mean here? | Having no name at all | Living under the sea | *Ruling itself and making its own choices | Being part of a bigger army
exercise: Self-driving cars have autonomy. What does this suggest? | They must always be pushed | *They can choose their own way without a driver | They can fly over the roads | They are painted bright colours
exercise: Ella reads, «Scotland has a degree of autonomy.» What does «a degree of autonomy» mean? | Complete control over everyone else | A large amount of money | No choices at all | *Some freedom to govern itself, but not complete freedom
test: Children gain autonomy as they grow up. What does gain autonomy mean? | Grow taller every year | *Get more chances to make their own choices | Stop learning new things at school | Lose their homes and their families
test: Which of these is an example of a region with autonomy within a country? | A cloud | The moon | *Scotland | A school bus
exam: Which sentence uses autonomy correctly? | The town ate its autonomy for lunch | The town was autonomy-coloured and very tall | *The town voted to make its own local laws, showing its autonomy | The autonomy of the town was a red bicycle
